WEBVTT

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:05.480
The end of the year already...

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:07.480
It sure did come fast!

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:10.760
Aoi-san, you'll be testing to get into a university
 in the new year, won't you?

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:15.240
Yes, although I'm still trying 
to figure out where I want to go.

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:18.220
Well, you still have time to decide.

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:21.250
It's good to give such things
 careful thought.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:23.830
Now, why don't we take a break?

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:24.530
Sure!

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:27.800
Your usual café au lait.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.500
Thank you.

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.010
<i>I'll be a university student next year, huh?</i>

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:39.750
Kiyotaka!

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:42.370
Owner! Welcome back.

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:43.830
Welcome back.

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:46.200
Oh, Aoi-chan's here too.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.020
That'll save time.

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:50.740
Wanna come to our house for New Year's?

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:52.560
We're havin' a competition!

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:12.960
<b>Holmes of Kyoto</b>

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:29.120
Episode 9

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:29.120
"The Sound of the Bell at Gion"

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:31.880
<b>Shinkyogoku</b>

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:35.760
A competition hosted by the owner?

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:36.880
It sounds like fun!

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:41.480
Grandfather must be vexed
 that people so enjoyed

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:44.040
the appraising game at 
Yanagihara-sensei's party.

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:47.640
They're like children, the way they compete.

00:02:47.990 --> 00:02:51.400
I just wish they'd stop dragging me into it.

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:54.240
On top of how busy I already am,

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.060
I now have to go shopping at Nishiki Market.

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:57.900
Don't worry.

00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:00.160
I'll help out!

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:01.660
I appreciate it.

00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:05.440
By the way, Aoi-san,

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:08.510
do you know about the 
Eight Holy Sites of Shinkyogoku?

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:09.300
No.

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:14.600
There are eight temples 
and shrines lining Shinkyogoku.

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:11.670
<b>1. Seiganji Temple</b>

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:12.670
<b>2. Seishin-in Temple</b>

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:13.670
<b>3. Torayakushi Saikoji Temple</b>

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:14.670
<b>4. Takoyakushi Eifukuji Temple</b>

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:18.920
Visiting them all is known 
as the Eight Holy Site Walk.

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:15.670
<b>5. Jienzan Anyoji Temple</b>

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:16.670
<b>6. Zenchoji Temple</b>

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:17.670
<b>7. Nishiki-Tenmangu Shrine</b>

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:18.920
<b>8. Somedono-in Temple</b>

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:21.900
If we're going as far as Nishiki Market,

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:23.410
why don't we visit them?

00:03:23.410 --> 00:03:25.180
Oh, that sounds great!

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:28.430
Then shall we start 
with the nearby Seiganji?

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:33.690
It's primarily used to pray for 
success in the performing arts.

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:37.470
Oh, wow. I hope Akihito-san pays a visit.

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:38.440
I agree.

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:40.300
I'm begging you, Buddha!

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:44.200
Let me become even more famous next year!

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:45.700
Is that...

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:48.520
Aoi-san, let's go visit the next one.

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:50.440
What? Ah, but—

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:54.040
Say! If it isn't Holmes and Aoi-chan!

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:56.610
It's been some time, Akihito-san.

00:04:00.570 --> 00:04:02.700
<b>Saikoji
Torayakushi</b>

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:11.450
<b>N i s h i k i   T e n m a n g u</b>

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:18.000
W-Wow, Nishiki Market really is crowded...

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.480
Yeah, it's a battlefield.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:21.380
Gosh...

00:04:22.310 --> 00:04:24.390
Holmes-san is just so knowledgeable, though.

00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:27.090
I can't believe there's a cafe 
like this in a marketplace.

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:29.490
The view from above is pretty nuts, huh?

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:32.150
Thank you very much.

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:33.000
Thanks!

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.130
Oh, this is good!

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:39.300
Of course, I like yours better.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:40.750
I'm flattered.

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:45.830
<i>I always have café au lait.</i>

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:50.160
<i>Holmes-san's coffee that everybody praises...</i>

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:52.010
<i>I'd like to try it too.</i>

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:55.010
Come on in.

00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:56.520
Don't mind if I do.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:00.020
That's right. Put the Muchas on the wall.

00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:04.280
Put the model in the bay window. 
Somewhere unobtrusive.

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:10.280
Not like that. It's a bit crooked.

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:12.860
Yoshie-san!

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:14.540
Oh, welcome back.

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:17.790
It's been quite a while,
Aoi-chan, Akihito-kun.

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:20.080
Hello there, Yoshie-san.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:22.300
You're looking as beautiful as ever today.

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:24.270
Thank you.

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:26.660
I watch you on TV all the time.

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:30.970
I couldn't be more honored 
to hear you say that!

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:33.560
Akihito-san seems to be 
under a misapprehension.

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:36.780
Yes, you told him that Rikyu-kun is her son,

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:38.310
but he didn't believe you.

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:41.440
It's funny though, so let's 
let him dangle a while longer.

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:43.760
What?

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:45.060
Oh, nothing.

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:48.320
You two just seem to get along so well.

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:51.830
<i>{m}Holmes-san's usual nastiness...</i>

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.820
The party will start soon.

00:05:54.430 --> 00:05:57.320
If there's anything you want to 
see before then, let me know.

00:05:58.020 --> 00:05:59.580
<i>{m}Anything I want to see?</i>

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:05.980
Okay! I want to see your room!

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:08.600
M-My room?

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:13.400
Wow, what a mess.

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:15.340
Didn't I warn you?

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:20.610
But you keep the store so clean...

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:22.820
That's because it's where I work.

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:25.730
But here is different.

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:28.490
This is my personal space.

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:30.630
When I wake up in the morning,

00:06:30.630 --> 00:06:33.180
I just reach out, and a book I 
want to read is right there.

00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:35.990
This is my ideal environment.

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:40.300
Incidentally, one of my special skills 
is the ability to reach into a stack

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:43.250
and immediately find the book I want.

00:06:45.910 --> 00:06:47.820
Feeling disillusioned?

00:06:50.490 --> 00:06:52.760
No. I'm a little relieved, actually.

00:06:53.090 --> 00:06:57.020
I always thought of you
 as such a perfectionist.

00:06:57.840 --> 00:06:59.520
Well, I think it's about time.

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:01.380
I need to get changed,

00:07:01.380 --> 00:07:03.190
so you should go ahead without me.

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:06.400
Man, I gotta say...

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:10.050
Dating a weirdo like him 
wouldn't be easy, would it?

00:07:10.050 --> 00:07:13.530
Huh?! Wh-Why are you asking me?

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:16.620
What do you really think, Aoi-chan?

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:18.310
Wh-What do I think?

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:21.290
I think he's just wonderful...

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:23.880
But there's no chance that

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:26.900
someone with such a refined sense 
of beauty would choose me.

00:07:26.900 --> 00:07:29.660
So I kind of assumed there 
was this line between us...

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:33.380
Well, I was more asking about
 his weirdo tendencies.

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:37.560
I think I get what you mean, though.

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:39.670
But he seems to think of you as someone

00:07:39.670 --> 00:07:43.200
who's gone through 
the same heartbreak he has.

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:45.620
Besides, he's a perfect 
gentleman to everyone.

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:49.190
Yeah... that's true.

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:55.570
So, what <i>do</i> you think about 
his weirdo tendencies?

00:07:55.570 --> 00:07:57.060
I'm used to them by now.

00:07:58.120 --> 00:07:59.200
Same here.

00:08:08.390 --> 00:08:10.710
She said these are Muchas, right?

00:08:11.060 --> 00:08:11.860
Yes.

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:14.610
We have the same ones at our house.

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:15.720
Rikyu-kun!

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:18.470
What's this about you having them?

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:23.480
The owner knows my mom loves
 lithographs, so he sent us these...

00:08:23.990 --> 00:08:26.480
with the message, 
"I'm always thinking of you."

00:08:27.180 --> 00:08:30.480
Then Mom gave him the same ones in return

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:34.280
with the message, 
"Please always keep thinking of me."

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:35.990
How wonderful.

00:08:36.190 --> 00:08:36.730
Huh?

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:40.440
Wait, so... your mom is dating the owner, then?

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:41.480
Yeah.

00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:43.250
So then...

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:45.320
Is she here?

00:08:45.320 --> 00:08:46.830
Of course she is.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:49.310
I told you before, didn't I?

00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:50.520
U-Um...

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:52.590
Oh, Rikyu, you made it!

00:08:53.080 --> 00:08:55.430
Did you say hello to your 
tea ceremony teacher for me?

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:57.970
Yeah, he sends his regards.

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:00.260
Though he could barely contain his drool...

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:03.150
Don't speak of him that way.

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:05.020
Sensei is a wonderful person.

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:07.730
Mom, you're really into old men, aren't you?

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:09.780
I'm so sorry.

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:12.990
My son is rather impudent, 
but I hope you can still be friends.

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:17.840
Well? You believe me now?

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:18.960
You're kidding...

00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:20.690
A-Akihito-san...

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:25.370
I can't believe Yoshie-san is into old men!

00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:26.290
<i>That's</i> the problem?

00:09:26.930 --> 00:09:28.250
Sorry for the wait.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:33.380
<i>Holmes-san...</i>

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:35.050
Oh? And what's wrong with you?

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:38.380
Holmes, you bastard! You kept this from me!

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:40.640
Whatever could you mean?

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:45.000
Hey, why does Yoshie-san like old guys?

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:47.250
Was your dad one, too?

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:50.200
No, he was younger than her.

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:51.400
For real?

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:55.160
He quit his job and messed around.
 And he cheated constantly.

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:58.660
He was the archetypal bad husband.

00:09:58.940 --> 00:10:01.450
She divorced him when I was little.

00:10:02.300 --> 00:10:03.660
Wow...

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:06.510
Soon after, Yoshie-san met my grandfather

00:10:06.510 --> 00:10:07.900
and they started dating.

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:11.920
I was happy because I got 
a little brother out of it.

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:15.580
And I was really happy 
I got to meet Kiyo-nii!

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:21.930
Well, it's 5 o'clock now. 
Let's kick things off.

00:10:22.280 --> 00:10:23.860
A toast to the past year,

00:10:23.860 --> 00:10:27.020
and to an even better one this year!

00:10:27.470 --> 00:10:28.440
Cheers!

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:30.310
Cheers!

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:35.070
Wow, I'm glad the owner kept 
things short this time.

00:10:35.390 --> 00:10:41.520
Praising Yanagihara-sensei's short toast
 in front of him must have paid off.

00:10:42.880 --> 00:10:45.830
Now, I think we'll start our little game.

00:10:46.190 --> 00:10:47.830
About time!

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:50.960
Allow me to explain the details.

00:10:51.510 --> 00:10:54.750
Today's game, presented by Yagashira Seiji,

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:56.840
will be a treasure hunt.

00:10:58.890 --> 00:11:03.410
You'll each be receiving a copy 
of a coded message I've written.

00:11:03.410 --> 00:11:07.600
You must decipher it in order 
to find a hidden golden key.

00:11:07.920 --> 00:11:10.600
The key is hidden somewhere on this floor.

00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:14.610
There are also hints to its location
hidden in various places.

00:11:15.180 --> 00:11:21.610
Whoever finds the key will receive both it
 and a present from my grandfather.

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:28.160
I helped with the setup, 
so I can't participate.

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:30.620
I see. That's too bad.

00:11:31.110 --> 00:11:36.240
"The maiden subject of Munch's gaze
 holds a time in her arms.

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:40.380
The people of the tiny 
country whisper, 'I turn.'

00:11:40.650 --> 00:11:44.270
The key for which you seek 
does not require a journey.

00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:46.390
It is waiting for you there."

00:11:46.630 --> 00:11:47.860
The heck does that mean?

00:11:47.860 --> 00:11:49.850
I can't make heads or tails of it!

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:51.000
What does it...

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:52.890
Aoi-chan, follow me!

00:12:02.680 --> 00:12:04.280
Why are we going upstairs?

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:07.530
He said the hints and the 
treasure were both downstairs.

00:12:07.530 --> 00:12:10.280
Aoi-chan, you really didn't notice?

00:12:10.900 --> 00:12:13.570
Remember when we were in his room earlier?

00:12:13.570 --> 00:12:18.670
He totally hid something 
on top of his dresser then.

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:22.520
It's probably some clue 
about what that message means!

00:12:22.520 --> 00:12:23.840
O-Oh...

00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:27.110
Holmes of Kyoto's Teramachi Sanjo...

00:12:27.110 --> 00:12:31.370
Kajiwara Akihito, the Kudo Shunsaku 
of Kyoto's Shijo Karasuma,

00:12:31.370 --> 00:12:33.440
is about to expose your secret!

00:12:35.090 --> 00:12:37.190
<i>What's a Kudo Shunsaku?</i>

00:12:41.880 --> 00:12:42.670
Uh oh!

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:52.200
<i>This is from...</i>

00:12:57.920 --> 00:12:59.880
He fixed it?

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:00.460
Why?

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:04.720
<b>Victory</b>

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:04.720
<i>Even the maple leaves... 
Ensho-san painted those.</i>

00:13:05.100 --> 00:13:06.720
<i>Does this mean Holmes-san...</i>

00:13:09.280 --> 00:13:11.310
<i>He just couldn't throw it away?</i>

00:13:23.330 --> 00:13:24.550
You...

00:13:24.550 --> 00:13:25.740
Ensho-san!

00:13:33.530 --> 00:13:34.750
Stop this.

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:36.500
Stop this at once.

00:13:37.100 --> 00:13:38.190
Holmes-san...

00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:39.880
Kiyo-nii...

00:13:40.350 --> 00:13:42.870
Now, don't go lookin' at me that way.

00:13:42.870 --> 00:13:44.630
It ain't like I snuck in.

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:48.510
I got Yagashira-sensei's permission,
 just like I should.

00:13:50.410 --> 00:13:51.510
Why are you here?

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:56.390
Now, now. At least give me a 
minute to explain the trick.

00:13:56.990 --> 00:14:02.500
"The subject of Munch's gaze" is referrin' to 
the sunset the man in <i>The Scream</i> is lookin' at.

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:06.780
"Sunset" takes us to Mucha's lithograph, 
<i>Rêverie du Soir</i>

00:14:07.230 --> 00:14:09.400
The time she holds is in the title—"Rêverie."

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:16.040
Specifically Debussy's "Rêverie," 
which takes four minutes to play.

00:14:16.510 --> 00:14:24.050
Next, the tiny country referred to in 
"the people of the tiny country whisper, 'I turn'"

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:28.050
is the world's smallest country, Vatican City.

00:14:28.530 --> 00:14:30.800
The official language 
of the Vatican is Latin.

00:14:31.130 --> 00:14:35.560
In Latin, "I turn" is "volvo."

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:35.550
<b>"I turn"</b>

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:41.040
And when you convert the four minutes
 of "Rêverie" into seconds...

00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:42.560
The Volvo 240.

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:46.320
I had high hopes knowin' it was you
 who designed the code,

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:48.600
but it was so simple, I'm disappointed.

00:14:48.600 --> 00:14:50.450
I'm terribly sorry.

00:14:50.710 --> 00:14:52.700
Had I known you'd be coming,

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:55.950
I would have customized 
it especially for you.

00:14:55.950 --> 00:14:57.450
I don't need this thing.

00:14:57.760 --> 00:15:00.020
I figured if I was attendin' your party,

00:15:00.020 --> 00:15:02.610
I'd prepare my own entertainment for ya.

00:15:02.610 --> 00:15:03.340
Entertainment?

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:09.690
That's right, Holmes-han... 
An appraisal game between you an' me.

00:15:09.690 --> 00:15:11.010
Very well.

00:15:20.090 --> 00:15:22.180
What are the hammer and knife for?

00:15:22.180 --> 00:15:25.270
Not for driving into your head, I suppose?

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:28.140
You sure do come up with some scary ideas...

00:15:28.140 --> 00:15:30.780
But no. If you think an item's fake, 
then use those to destroy it.

00:15:31.150 --> 00:15:32.680
Very well.

00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:35.280
That'd be a fine way to work off some stress.

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:37.040
Can say that again.

00:15:39.760 --> 00:15:42.000
Those are Raku tea bowls.

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:42.540
Yeah.

00:15:42.900 --> 00:15:45.290
Determine which is the real one.

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:54.050
<i>They both look the same to me.</i>

00:15:58.680 --> 00:16:00.680
<i>Is the right one the counterfeit?</i>

00:16:02.680 --> 00:16:03.560
Huh?

00:16:11.120 --> 00:16:13.960
I'm sorry to say it, but they were both fakes.

00:16:13.960 --> 00:16:17.800
Though in fine imitation of the style of
 Keinyu, eleventh heir to the House of Raku.

00:16:17.800 --> 00:16:22.000
Aw, I thought that makin' two 
of 'em would throw ya off.

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:25.770
I'd had high hopes knowin'
 it was you who made 'em,

00:16:25.770 --> 00:16:28.210
but it was so simple, I'm disappointed.

00:16:28.570 --> 00:16:31.030
You're as implacable as ever.

00:16:31.030 --> 00:16:32.470
Now, what about this?

00:16:35.320 --> 00:16:38.250
Yamaoka Tesshu's "Good and Evil."

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:40.970
A disagreeable choice of subject.

00:16:41.460 --> 00:16:43.140
You wrote it very well,

00:16:43.140 --> 00:16:45.480
but I can still see you 
here and there in places.

00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:50.200
What, they're all fakes?

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:52.240
Beg your pardon for the long openin' act.

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:54.740
Here's the grand finale.

00:16:58.820 --> 00:17:02.560
An ukiyo-e by Sharaku, <i>Ichikawa Omezo</i>.

00:17:03.340 --> 00:17:07.130
That's right. And it's a painting, not a print.

00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:11.130
<i>A Sharaku painting...</i>

00:17:11.740 --> 00:17:14.730
Sharaku is known as "the mysterious painter."

00:17:14.730 --> 00:17:17.140
He only created for a short time, 
and made very few pieces.

00:17:17.400 --> 00:17:20.020
His one-of-a-kind paintings...

00:17:20.020 --> 00:17:22.230
I expect they would fetch 
hundreds of millions.

00:17:45.300 --> 00:17:46.540
Sorry to tell ya...

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:48.040
That one was real.

00:17:49.410 --> 00:17:50.680
For real?!

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:52.800
No way... Kiyo-nii lost?

00:17:55.590 --> 00:17:59.830
Anything can happen in this world.

00:17:59.830 --> 00:18:04.430
What you just cut in half was an 
honest-to-goodness Sharaku painting.

00:18:04.840 --> 00:18:09.940
Of course, Sharaku don't mean 
anythin' to me. Nothin' does.

00:18:13.040 --> 00:18:15.850
<i>That piece... was real?</i>

00:18:23.240 --> 00:18:25.950
Just kiddin'! It was all just a joke.

00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:27.960
A joke?

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:32.070
That was a counterfeit I made,
 just like the rest.

00:18:32.070 --> 00:18:38.470
But the way you flinched when I said it was 
real... Your expression was a masterpiece!

00:18:38.940 --> 00:18:41.450
You sure are adorable.

00:18:41.450 --> 00:18:44.880
Were you sure it wasn't real?

00:18:44.880 --> 00:18:47.020
I wanna hear it from you personally.

00:18:50.030 --> 00:18:54.980
Perhaps I should break this impudent hand.

00:18:57.260 --> 00:18:59.820
You're as violent a child as ever.

00:19:00.670 --> 00:19:03.060
What was it that gave me away?

00:19:03.820 --> 00:19:04.990
Ah, I get it.

00:19:05.380 --> 00:19:09.040
Why did you choose Sharaku for this match?

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:10.270
Why?

00:19:10.270 --> 00:19:12.730
Sharaku, the mysterious painter...

00:19:12.730 --> 00:19:16.300
Were you trying to superimpose 
your life over his?

00:19:17.540 --> 00:19:21.590
Did you want me to hear 
that cry from your heart?

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:23.760
"I'm the one who painted this!"

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:28.770
Your inner self is just like a child...
 It's truly adorable.

00:19:29.200 --> 00:19:31.520
You really are one smart-mouthed brat!

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:34.770
Such an immature way to react to the truth...

00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:42.030
Stop this!

00:19:44.420 --> 00:19:48.290
This is a party, you two! Stop it already!

00:19:51.640 --> 00:19:53.540
Your game's over, right?

00:19:54.610 --> 00:19:57.910
Ensho-san, would you please clean this up?

00:19:57.910 --> 00:19:59.050
I'd appreciate it.

00:20:03.560 --> 00:20:05.520
Yeah, the little lady's right.

00:20:05.520 --> 00:20:07.060
Beggin' your pardon.

00:20:07.480 --> 00:20:12.050
But this ain't over. 
'Cause I really don't like ya.

00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:16.060
So much that I wanna 
tear you limb from limb.

00:20:16.960 --> 00:20:20.780
Next time we meet,
I'm really gonna crush ya.

00:20:26.630 --> 00:20:29.560
Aoi-san, I'm sorry about all that.

00:20:29.560 --> 00:20:33.080
N-No... I'm the one 
who panicked and stepped in.

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:37.920
Holmes, you feel a little better after that?

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:43.480
I do. That Sharaku was
 astonishingly well done.

00:20:43.480 --> 00:20:45.280
But you saw through it?

00:20:45.280 --> 00:20:47.200
The ear was wrong.

00:20:47.200 --> 00:20:48.470
The ear?

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:52.760
Sharaku had a habit of drawing 
ears with five strokes.

00:20:52.760 --> 00:20:55.650
Ensho did his the same way,

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:57.910
but it didn't feel like habit.

00:20:57.910 --> 00:21:00.480
His version wasn't natural or effortless.

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:03.960
In other words, the ear felt like Ensho-san?

00:21:03.960 --> 00:21:04.700
Yes.

00:21:05.130 --> 00:21:08.070
But because of my moment's hesitation,

00:21:08.070 --> 00:21:09.990
I cannot call it a total victory.

00:21:10.230 --> 00:21:12.870
Yeah, you really froze up.

00:21:12.870 --> 00:21:13.870
Yes...

00:21:14.280 --> 00:21:16.870
Happy New Year!

00:21:17.150 --> 00:21:18.680
Here's to another year together!

00:21:18.680 --> 00:21:20.240
Preferably in moderation.

00:21:20.240 --> 00:21:22.880
Aw, don't be such a stranger!

00:21:23.230 --> 00:21:27.600
Incidentally, my resolution this year is to be
 bolder, both in my public and private lives!

00:21:27.600 --> 00:21:29.520
That sounds very much like you.

00:21:29.520 --> 00:21:30.500
And you, Aoi-san?

00:21:30.500 --> 00:21:31.890
Huh? Me?

00:21:33.130 --> 00:21:38.020
Okay, how about this? I want 
to get into drinking black coffee!

00:21:41.720 --> 00:21:43.680
Wh-Why are you laughing?!

00:21:43.680 --> 00:21:45.410
Was that worth a resolution?

00:21:45.410 --> 00:21:48.110
Aoi-san, I see you're 
trying to become an adult.

00:21:48.110 --> 00:21:51.030
I-It's not that big a deal...

00:21:51.030 --> 00:21:54.010
Anyway, what's your resolution, Holmes?

00:21:54.010 --> 00:21:55.540
Let's see...

00:21:56.120 --> 00:21:59.280
I was rather pathetic last year.

00:21:59.280 --> 00:22:01.720
So this year... you know?

00:22:01.720 --> 00:22:02.800
Do your best!

00:22:04.640 --> 00:22:05.430
I will.

00:22:07.320 --> 00:22:14.290
<b>Holmes of Kyoto</b>

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:51.380
Next Episode

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:51.380
"The Bisque Doll's Smile"

00:23:36.850 --> 00:23:40.310
The doll in the store is scary.

00:23:40.310 --> 00:23:42.990
Shall I tell you the story behind it?

00:23:42.990 --> 00:23:44.730
Nothing scary!

00:23:45.280 --> 00:23:48.040
Next time: "The Bisque Doll's Smile."

00:23:48.040 --> 00:23:50.300
Holmes-san, you really are nasty.
